# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to tune the configuration options for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Paano i-tune ang mga opsyon sa configuration para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to tune the configuration options"
msgstr "Paano i-tune ang mga opsyon sa configuration"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bounds computation is exact in principle but approximate in practice: evolving a Pauli error\n"
"term through a circuit produces an operator with exponentially many terms, and finding the spectral\n"
"norm of the resulting commutator is itself expensive. The options below control that cost. They fall\n"
"into three groups:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagkalkula ng mga bound ay eksakto sa prinsipyo pero approximate sa praktika: ang pag-evolve ng isang Pauli error\n"
"term sa isang circuit ay gumagawa ng operator na may exponentially na dami ng term, at ang paghahanap ng spectral\n"
"norm ng nagreresultang commutator ay magastos din mismo. Kinokontrol ng mga opsyon sa ibaba ang gastos na iyon. Nahahati sila\n"
"sa tatlong grupo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Accuracy** options change the numerical value of the bounds, trading tightness for cost.\n"
msgstr "Binabago ng mga opsyon sa **Accuracy** ang numerikal na halaga ng mga bound, kapalit ng higpit para sa mas mababang gastos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Scope** determines *which* bounds are computed.\n"
msgstr "Tinutukoy ng **Scope** *kung aling* mga bound ang kakalkulahin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Execution** options change *how* the computation runs (not what it computes).\n"
msgstr "Binabago ng mga opsyon sa **Execution** *kung paano* tumatakbo ang pagkalkula (hindi kung ano ang kinakalkula nito).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Option | Default | Controls | Effect on the result |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| **Accuracy** | | | |\n"
"| `evolution_max_terms` | `1_000_000` | How many operator terms survive the evolution | Lower: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `atol_simplify` | `1e-8` | Which commutator terms are discarded as negligible | Higher: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `eigval_max_qubits` | `14` | How wide a commutator can be for its spectral norm to be computed | Lower: cheaper, looser bounds |\n"
"| `atol_eigenvalue` | `1e-10` | When the iterative eigensolver counts as converged | Higher: cheaper, less accurate bounds |\n"
"| **Scope** | | | |\n"
"| `max_num_boxes` | `None` | How many boxes have bounds computed | Boxes beyond the limit keep the trivial bound of 2.0 |\n"
"| **Execution** | | | |\n"
"| `timeout` | `None` | A wall-clock budget for the whole computation | Any remaining work keeps the trivial bound of 2.0 |\n"
"| `num_processes` | `1` | How many worker processes compute bounds in parallel | None on its own |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Opsyon | Default | Kinokontrol | Epekto sa resulta |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| **Accuracy** | | | |\n"
"| `evolution_max_terms` | `1_000_000` | Ilang operator term ang natitira pagkatapos ng evolution | Mas mababa: mas mura, mas maluwag na mga bound |\n"
"| `atol_simplify` | `1e-8` | Aling mga commutator term ang itinatapon bilang bale-wala | Mas mataas: mas mura, mas maluwag na mga bound |\n"
"| `eigval_max_qubits` | `14` | Gaano kalapad ang commutator para makalkula ang spectral norm nito | Mas mababa: mas mura, mas maluwag na mga bound |\n"
"| `atol_eigenvalue` | `1e-10` | Kailan ituturing na nag-converge ang iterative eigensolver | Mas mataas: mas mura, mas di-tumpak na mga bound |\n"
"| **Scope** | | | |\n"
"| `max_num_boxes` | `None` | Ilang box ang kakalkulahan ng mga bound | Ang mga box na lampas sa limitasyon ay nananatili sa trivial na bound na 2.0 |\n"
"| **Execution** | | | |\n"
"| `timeout` | `None` | Isang wall-clock na badyet para sa buong pagkalkula | Anumang natitirang trabaho ay nananatili sa trivial na bound na 2.0 |\n"
"| `num_processes` | `1` | Ilang worker process ang sabay-sabay na kumakalkula ng mga bound | Wala sa sarili nito |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A bound is only useful if it is *valid*: it must never understate an error term's effect on the\n"
"observable. Loosening any of these options other than `atol_eigenvalue` can only make the bounds\n"
"larger (more conservative), never smaller. Thus, the cost of a loose setting is a larger sampling\n"
"overhead, not a wrong expectation value - [`atol_eigenvalue`](#atol_eigenvalue) is the exception.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapaki-pakinabang lang ang isang bound kung *valid* ito: hindi nito dapat maliitin ang epekto ng isang error term sa\n"
"observable. Ang pagluwag sa alinman sa mga opsyong ito maliban sa `atol_eigenvalue` ay makakapagpalaki lang sa mga bound\n"
"(mas konserbatibo), hindi kailanman magpapaliit. Kaya, ang kapalit ng maluwag na setting ay mas malaking sampling\n"
"overhead, hindi maling expectation value - ang [`atol_eigenvalue`](#atol_eigenvalue) ang eksepsiyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit definition {#circuit-definition}"
msgstr "Kahulugan ng circuit {#circuit-definition}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following experiments use the same Trotterized Ising circuit and observable as the [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart). At\n"
"this size, every option has a visible effect while each computation still takes less than a second.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang mga sumusunod na eksperimento ng parehong Trotterized Ising circuit at observable gaya ng [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart). Sa\n"
"laking ito, may nakikitang epekto ang bawat opsyon habang wala pang isang segundo ang bawat pagkalkula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A small helper summarizes each set of bounds in one line, so the effect of an option shows up as a\n"
"few numbers rather than a wall of arrays.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinubuod ng isang maliit na helper ang bawat set ng mga bound sa isang linya, kaya ang epekto ng isang opsyon ay lalabas bilang\n"
"ilang numero sa halip na isang pader ng mga array.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every bound lies between 0 and the trivial bound of 2.0. The summary reports the mean bound and its\n"
"standard deviation, followed by how the terms fall into these groups:\n"
"    - Terms bounded by exactly 0 because they commute with the evolved observable\n"
"    - Terms with a bound computed between 0 and 2.0\n"
"    - Terms left at the trivial 2.0\n"
msgstr ""
"Bawat bound ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at ng trivial na bound na 2.0. Iniuulat ng buod ang mean na bound at ang\n"
"standard deviation nito, kasunod kung paano nahahati ang mga term sa mga grupong ito:\n"
"    - Mga term na may bound na eksaktong 0 dahil nagko-commute sila sa na-evolve na observable\n"
"    - Mga term na may nakalkulang bound sa pagitan ng 0 at 2.0\n"
"    - Mga term na nanatili sa trivial na 2.0\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that **a lower mean is tighter, and tighter means a smaller sampling overhead later.**\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na **ang mas mababang mean ay mas mahigpit, at ang mas mahigpit ay nangangahulugang mas maliit na sampling overhead sa dakong huli.**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A sweep over one option marks the option's default with `*`:\n"
msgstr "Minamarkahan ng sweep sa isang opsyon ang default ng opsyon gamit ang `*`:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accuracy {#accuracy}"
msgstr "Katumpakan {#accuracy}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`evolution_max_terms` {#evolution-max-terms}"
msgstr "`evolution_max_terms` {#evolution-max-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evolving a Pauli error term through non-Clifford gates turns it into a sum of Paulis, and that sum\n"
"grows with circuit depth. `evolution_max_terms` caps how many of those terms are kept. The 1-norm of\n"
"whatever is discarded is added to the bound, so nothing is silently lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-evolve ng Pauli error term sa mga non-Clifford gate ay ginagawa itong kabuuan ng mga Pauli, at lumalaki ang kabuuang iyon\n"
"kasabay ng lalim ng circuit. Nililimitahan ng `evolution_max_terms` kung ilan sa mga term na iyon ang itatabi. Ang 1-norm ng\n"
"anumang itinapon ay idinaragdag sa bound, kaya walang tahimik na nawawala.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sweep runs from tighter than the default down to an extreme cut. Lowering the cap makes the\n"
"computation cheaper and the bounds looser.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tumatakbo ang sweep mula sa mas mahigpit kaysa sa default pababa sa matinding pagputol. Ang pagbaba ng cap ay ginagawang mas mura ang\n"
"pagkalkula at mas maluwag ang mga bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Raising the cap past its default changes nothing here. For a circuit of this size, the default\n"
"already keeps every term, so the bounds are as tight as this option can make them. That is the\n"
"typical situation. Tightening an accuracy option only pays off once its default is actually limiting,\n"
"and the way to find out is the experiment above. Rerun it with a tighter value and see whether the\n"
"bounds move.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtaas ng cap nang lampas sa default ay walang binabago dito. Para sa circuit na ganito kalaki, ang default\n"
"ay nagtatabi na ng bawat term, kaya ang mga bound ay kasinghigpit na ng magagawa ng opsyong ito. Iyon ang\n"
"tipikal na sitwasyon. Ang paghigpit sa isang accuracy option ay may saysay lang kapag ang default nito ay talagang naglilimita,\n"
"at ang paraan para malaman iyon ay ang eksperimento sa itaas. Patakbuhin ulit ito gamit ang mas mahigpit na halaga at tingnan kung gumalaw ang mga\n"
"bound.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-warning\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Warning:** The underlying propagation routine treats `evolution_max_terms` as a *capacity to\n"
"pre-allocate*, not as an upper limit to check against. Passing something nominally unlimited, such\n"
"as `numpy.iinfo(numpy.uint).max`, asks the allocator for terabytes of memory and aborts the process.\n"
"Keep it to a realistic number. The default of one million is already generous.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Babala:** Itinuturing ng pinagbabatayang propagation routine ang `evolution_max_terms` bilang *capacity na\n"
"i-pre-allocate*, hindi bilang upper limit na susuriin. Ang pagpasa ng nominal na walang limitasyon, gaya\n"
"ng `numpy.iinfo(numpy.uint).max`, ay humihingi sa allocator ng terabytes ng memory at ina-abort ang process.\n"
"Panatilihin ito sa makatotohanang numero. Sapat na ang default na isang milyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</div>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`atol_simplify` {#atol-simplify}"
msgstr "`atol_simplify` {#atol-simplify}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the commutator is formed, terms with a coefficient below `atol_simplify` are dropped. As with\n"
"the evolution cap, the 1-norm lost this way is added to the bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkabuo ng commutator, itinatapon ang mga term na may coefficient na mas mababa sa `atol_simplify`. Gaya ng\n"
"evolution cap, ang 1-norm na nawala sa ganitong paraan ay idinaragdag sa bound.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`eigval_max_qubits` {#eigval-max-qubits}"
msgstr "`eigval_max_qubits` {#eigval-max-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tightest available bound is the spectral norm of the commutator, which needs an eigenvalue\n"
"computation. That becomes expensive as the commutator widens, so `eigval_max_qubits` sets the width\n"
"beyond which the attempt is abandoned in favour of the triangle inequality. That bound,\n"
"$2 \\sum_i |c_i|$ over the commutator's coefficients $c_i$, is valid but looser.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinakamahigpit na magagamit na bound ay ang spectral norm ng commutator, na nangangailangan ng eigenvalue\n"
"na pagkalkula. Nagiging magastos iyon habang lumalapad ang commutator, kaya itinatakda ng `eigval_max_qubits` ang lapad\n"
"na lampas dito ay iiwan ang pagtatangka pabor sa triangle inequality. Ang bound na iyon,\n"
"$2 \\sum_i |c_i|$ sa mga coefficient $c_i$ ng commutator, ay valid pero mas maluwag.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting it to zero forces the fallback everywhere, which shows the benefit of the eigensolver\n"
"in one number.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtatakda nito sa zero ay pumipilit sa fallback saanman, na nagpapakita ng benepisyo ng eigensolver\n"
"sa iisang numero.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even with the eigensolver switched off, the mean stays far below the trivial 2.0. The share\n"
"of terms bounded by 0 does not change: a term that commutes exactly with the evolved observable\n"
"has a zero commutator, which is recognized before any eigenvalue computation is considered. Of the\n"
"others, the triangle-inequality bound reaches 2.0 for some and is capped there, but for many it is\n"
"still smaller, so they keep a computed bound below 2.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit naka-off ang eigensolver, nananatiling mas mababa nang malayo ang mean sa trivial na 2.0. Ang bahagi\n"
"ng mga term na may bound na 0 ay hindi nagbabago: ang term na eksaktong nagko-commute sa na-evolve na observable\n"
"ay may zero na commutator, na nakikilala bago pa isaalang-alang ang anumang eigenvalue na pagkalkula. Sa\n"
"iba, ang triangle-inequality bound ay umaabot sa 2.0 para sa ilan at doon na-cap, pero para sa marami ay\n"
"mas maliit pa rin ito, kaya nananatili silang may nakalkulang bound na mas mababa sa 2.0.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`atol_eigenvalue` {#atol-eigenvalue}"
msgstr "`atol_eigenvalue` {#atol-eigenvalue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the spectral norm *is* computed, `atol_eigenvalue` is the convergence tolerance of the\n"
"iterative eigensolver. Most commutators never reach that solver, though:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag *kinakalkula* ang spectral norm, ang `atol_eigenvalue` ang convergence tolerance ng\n"
"iterative eigensolver. Karamihan ng mga commutator ay hindi umaabot sa solver na iyon, gayunpaman:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A commutator acting on at most four qubits is diagonalized exactly, directly.\n"
msgstr "Ang commutator na kumikilos sa hindi hihigit sa apat na qubit ay dinidiagonalize nang eksakto, direkta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A wider one is first reduced to the smallest number of qubits that its Pauli terms need,\n"
"and if that reduced form acts on at most eight qubits, it is diagonalized exactly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mas malapad ay unang binabawasan sa pinakamaliit na bilang ng mga qubit na kailangan ng mga Pauli term nito,\n"
"at kung ang nabawasang anyo ay kumikilos sa hindi hihigit sa walong qubit, dinidiagonalize ito nang eksakto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only a commutator that still needs more than eight qubits after that reduction goes to the iterative\n"
"solver, which is the only place this tolerance applies. Circuits of the size used in this guide never get\n"
"that far, so a sweep over this option would show identical bounds for every value. It matters for\n"
"wide light cones on large devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tanging ang commutator na nangangailangan pa rin ng higit sa walong qubit pagkatapos ng pagbabawas na iyon ang pupunta sa iterative\n"
"solver, na siyang tanging lugar kung saan nalalapat ang tolerance na ito. Ang mga circuit na kasinglaki ng gamit sa gabay na ito ay hindi kailanman\n"
"umaabot doon, kaya ang sweep sa opsyong ito ay magpapakita ng magkakaparehong bound para sa bawat halaga. Mahalaga ito para sa\n"
"malalapad na light cone sa malalaking device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike the other accuracy options, loosening `atol_eigenvalue` is *not* safe in one direction. An\n"
"iterative eigensolver approaches the extremal eigenvalue from inside the spectrum, so an estimate\n"
"that has not fully converged understates the spectral norm, and the bound. The default is\n"
"deliberately tight for that reason. If the solver fails to converge, the triangle-inequality\n"
"fallback takes over, which is valid again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi tulad ng ibang accuracy option, ang pagluwag sa `atol_eigenvalue` ay *hindi* ligtas sa isang direksyon. Ang\n"
"iterative eigensolver ay lumalapit sa extremal na eigenvalue mula sa loob ng spectrum, kaya ang estimate\n"
"na hindi pa ganap na nag-converge ay nagmamaliit sa spectral norm, at sa bound. Sadyang mahigpit ang default\n"
"dahil doon. Kung hindi mag-converge ang solver, papalit ang triangle-inequality\n"
"fallback, na valid ulit.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scope {#scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw {#scope}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_num_boxes` {#max-num-boxes}"
msgstr "`max_num_boxes` {#max-num-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes the useful limit is not accuracy but depth. `max_num_boxes` stops spawning bound\n"
"computations past a given number of boxes, and every layer beyond it is assigned the trivial bound\n"
"of 2.0 instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Minsan ang kapaki-pakinabang na limitasyon ay hindi accuracy kundi lalim. Ang `max_num_boxes` ay humihinto sa pagsisimula ng mga bound\n"
"na pagkalkula lampas sa isang tiyak na bilang ng mga box, at bawat layer na lampas dito ay binibigyan ng trivial na bound\n"
"na 2.0 sa halip.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The limit counts the noisy `BoxOp` instructions (those carrying an `InjectNoise` annotation) rather\n"
"than, for example, a depth in gates. That keeps it tied to the user-visible structure of the circuit and\n"
"avoids coupling to the auto-generated annotation references, which can change between\n"
"transpilation runs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binibilang ng limitasyon ang mga maingay na `BoxOp` na instruction (yaong may dalang `InjectNoise` annotation) sa halip\n"
"na, halimbawa, lalim sa mga gate. Pinapanatili nitong nakatali ito sa istrukturang nakikita ng user ng circuit at\n"
"iniiwasan ang pagkakabit sa mga auto-generated na annotation reference, na maaaring magbago sa pagitan ng\n"
"mga transpilation run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the natural choice for a circuit whose two halves are handled by forward and backward bounds\n"
"respectively: compute each only as deep as it will be used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang natural na pagpipilian para sa circuit na ang dalawang kalahati ay hinahawakan ng forward at backward na mga bound\n"
"ayon sa pagkakasunod: kalkulahin ang bawat isa hanggang sa lalim lang na gagamitin.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution {#execution}"
msgstr "Pagpapatupad {#execution}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`timeout` {#timeout}"
msgstr "`timeout` {#timeout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`timeout` is a wall-clock budget in seconds. When it expires, the bounds that have been computed are kept\n"
"and everything outstanding keeps the trivial bound of 2.0, so the result is always usable, just\n"
"looser the earlier you cut it off.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `timeout` ay wall-clock na badyet sa mga segundo. Kapag nag-expire ito, itatabi ang mga bound na nakalkula na\n"
"at ang lahat ng nakabinbin ay mananatili sa trivial na bound na 2.0, kaya laging magagamit ang resulta, mas\n"
"maluwag lang kapag mas maaga mo itong pinutol.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is not a hard deadline: already-running tasks are allowed to finish, so the call can overrun the\n"
"budget by the duration of one task.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi ito mahigpit na deadline: pinapayagang matapos ang mga gawaing tumatakbo na, kaya maaaring lumampas ang tawag sa\n"
"badyet nang hanggang tagal ng isang gawain.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes` {#num-processes}"
msgstr "`num_processes` {#num-processes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bounds for different error terms are independent, so `num_processes` distributes them over worker\n"
"processes. On its own, this affects only how long the computation takes, never its result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga bound para sa magkakaibang error term ay independent, kaya ipinamamahagi sila ng `num_processes` sa mga worker\n"
"process. Sa sarili nito, ang naaapektuhan lang ay kung gaano katagal ang pagkalkula, hindi kailanman ang resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** A `timeout` combined with `num_processes` makes the result depend on timing: which tasks\n"
"finish before the budget expires is not deterministic. The bounds stay valid, but they are no longer\n"
"reproducible from run to run.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandaan:** Ang `timeout` na isinama sa `num_processes` ay nagpapadepende sa resulta sa timing: kung aling mga gawain\n"
"ang matatapos bago mag-expire ang badyet ay hindi deterministic. Nananatiling valid ang mga bound, pero hindi na sila\n"
"mauulit sa bawat run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where to start {#where-to-start}"
msgstr "Saan magsisimula {#where-to-start}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The defaults are chosen to give tight bounds on circuits of a size where that is affordable. When a\n"
"computation is too slow, try applying the options in roughly this order:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinili ang mga default para magbigay ng mahigpit na mga bound sa mga circuit na may sukat kung saan abot-kaya iyon. Kapag\n"
"masyadong mabagal ang isang pagkalkula, subukang ilapat ang mga opsyon sa humigit-kumulang na ganitong pagkakasunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes`: A free speed-up, with no accuracy cost.\n"
msgstr "`num_processes`: Libreng pagpapabilis, walang gastos sa accuracy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_num_boxes`: If you know in advance how deep into the circuit you care about.\n"
msgstr "`max_num_boxes`: Kung alam mo na nang maaga kung gaano kalalim sa circuit ang mahalaga sa iyo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`eigval_max_qubits`: Skips the most expensive step for the widest commutators, which are usually\n"
"a small minority of the terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"`eigval_max_qubits`: Nilalaktawan ang pinakamahal na hakbang para sa pinakamalalapad na commutator, na karaniwang\n"
"maliit na minorya ng mga term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`evolution_max_terms` and `atol_simplify`: These impact accuracy throughout, so tune\n"
"them last, checking with a sweep like the ones above to determine how far the bounds move.\n"
msgstr ""
"`evolution_max_terms` at `atol_simplify`: Nakakaapekto ang mga ito sa accuracy sa kabuuan, kaya i-tune\n"
"ang mga ito sa huli, at suriin gamit ang sweep na tulad ng nasa itaas para malaman kung gaano gumagalaw ang mga bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`timeout`: A hard stop rather than a tuning aid, for when a computation must finish by a deadline,\n"
"whatever the quality.\n"
msgstr ""
"`timeout`: Isang hard stop sa halip na tulong sa pag-tune, para kapag kailangang matapos ang pagkalkula bago ang deadline,\n"
"anuman ang kalidad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The looser the bounds, the larger the sampling overhead that `compute_local_scales` will report for\n"
"a given bias tolerance. That overhead is the quantity worth watching while tuning: it tells you what\n"
"the approximations actually cost.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang mas maluwag ang mga bound, mas malaki ang sampling overhead na iuulat ng `compute_local_scales` para sa\n"
"ibinigay na bias tolerance. Ang overhead na iyon ang dapat bantayan habang nagt-tune: sinasabi nito kung ano\n"
"ang aktwal na halaga ng mga approximation.\n"
